(window.COURSE_SOURCES = window.COURSE_SOURCES || {})["personal-training"] = "## Sources note\n\nWhich sources were read, and how far. Written 11/10/2026.\n\n**Read in full (body text)**\n- WHO 2020 guidelines on physical activity and sedentary behaviour (Bull et al., BJSM 2020).\n- Morton et al. 2018, protein supplementation and resistance training (BJSM).\n- Swinton, Schoenfeld and Murphy 2024, dose-response modelling of resistance exercise (Sports Medicine, PMC full text).\n\n**Read in part**\n- Whitfield et al. 2017, ACSM preparticipation screening algorithm: abstract, introduction, methods and the algorithm figure notes. The results tables were not read in detail; the referral percentages come from the abstract and introduction.\n- Rubak et al. 2005, motivational interviewing: abstract, results excerpt and introduction opening. The full methods and tables were not read.\n- Ng et al. 2012, self-determination theory in health: abstract and excerpts (method, results summary, discussion). Not read in full.\n\n**Abstract only (full text paywalled or not opened)**\n- Schoenfeld, Ogborn and Krieger 2017, weekly volume and muscle mass.\n- Robinson et al. 2024, proximity to failure meta-regressions.\n- UK Chief Medical Officers' guidelines page: only the update history was read. The course tells the learner to check the current wording.\n\n**Not verified**\n- PAR-Q+ form, CIMSPA standards and REPs Ireland code of ethics: search links only, pages not opened.\n- No specific video was verified. The video entry is a search link.\n\n**Our inference or framing (labelled in the lessons)**\n- The 2-to-1 trade of vigorous for moderate minutes (derived from 75 versus 150).\n- The three scope zones, the consultation outline, the 60-minute session split, the 8-week Day A and Day B template, the double-progression and deload rules, RIR targets for beginners, and the set-count starting range.\n- The RIR teaching defaults, the talk test and the four MI skills are common teaching shorthand, not findings from the sources read.\n\n**Illustrative numbers**\nAll client cases (Sam, the four screening clients, the ramps) are invented.\n";
